From 6ef2490a1cb09ad9c604c466d44944d8e9f2bd50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kamalbuilds <geniusamansingh@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:22:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(solidcash): pick an external data NFT by its index tag,
 not by vout

A read of another stateful contract co-spends its data NFTs and re-creates them in the reader's
transaction, so only the NFTs the read needs move, and their vouts there need not be below the
vouts of the ones left in the owner's own transaction. _findExternalDataNft sorted every data NFT at
the owner's data-NFT address by vout and took position nftIndex, so after one read it could return
the wrong NFT (index 1 for index 0), and the next read failed with OP_VERIFY although the owner's
state had not changed. Use StateReader.findDataNfts with the external's own layout, which orders an
index-tagged layout by the tag in each commitment and keeps vout order for an untagged singleton.
---
 .../src/stateful/StatefulContract.ts          |  11 +-
 .../e2e/ExternalReadRelocatedDataNft.test.ts  | 108 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 117 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 packages/solidcash/test/e2e/ExternalReadRelocatedDataNft.test.ts

diff --git a/packages/solidcash/src/stateful/StatefulContract.ts b/packages/solidcash/src/stateful/StatefulContract.ts
index 05c5273ab..c6ef54cf6 100644
--- a/packages/solidcash/src/stateful/StatefulContract.ts
+++ b/packages/solidcash/src/stateful/StatefulContract.ts
@@ -175,7 +175,9 @@ import {
